WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.490
METE ATAMEL: Istio
is an open platform

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.700
to connect, manage, and
secure microservices.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.490
Let's see what it takes
to install and run

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:11.490
Istio on Google
Kubernetes Engine, or GKE.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.320
First, create a
Kubernetes cluster

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.470
on GKE with G Cloud Container
Clusters Create command.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.900
Make sure your cluster is
using Kubernetes 1.9 or newer,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.190
and grant admin permissions
to the current G Cloud user.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.290
Now, download the
latest Istio version

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.130
and add Istio CTL command
line tool to your path.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.160
Now we are ready to install
Istio's core components.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.740
We will install the
optional auth components.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.130
This creates Istio
system namespace

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:48.730
and deploys the four primary
control plane components--

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.110
Pilot, Mixer, Ingress,
and Certificate Authority.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.410
Let's quickly verify
the installation.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:57.350
And that's it.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.660
That's all it takes to
install Istio in GKE.

